earth: the friend you went into business with has taken the clients and the money
scene: The shared account is empty, the client list has gone, and {friend}'s phone goes straight to voicemail. Ten years of friendship, and a note on the desk that says only: sorry.
scene W: {N} trusted {friend} with a key, a signature and a share of everything. There are laws for exactly this, and {N} intends to use them.
scene U: {N} sits up all night with the bank statements, tracing each transfer back, looking for the month when {friend} decided.
scene B: {N} let {friend} hold the money because it was convenient. That was a mistake, and {N} does not make the same mistake twice.
scene R: The money and the clients are gone, and {N} drives straight to {friend}'s house with the radio off, heart pounding, hands tight on the wheel.
scene G: Now that {friend} has gone with the money, {N} remembers a feeling from years ago, deep down, and ignored. The feeling was right.
